ity of a No Deal  brexit you just undermine his position  don't you in trying to actually get the  sort of deal which he thinks would be  good for this country no because there  are two different things  one is leaving with in a way that is if  we do leave that it's not no deal and  then the second part which is the  difficult bit we haven't even started is  negotiating the future relationship and  that so the two things mixing them up is  actually not how the process works so  they are two completely separate thing  one is leaving and the other is actually  then negotiating over if we were to get  a deal over the next two years or so or  however long it takes to get that future  relationship but he has said he wants a  deal and by taking no deal off the table  that does weak in his hand doesn't it  they can just turn around and say you've  got a deal and we're not going to change  it which is although said so far well  yes and I don't know who exactly is  negotiating with because there's nobody  sitting in European in the commission  till November so the idea that there's a  lot of bluster and propaganda going on  here and from our point of view we've  just taken one off the table they've  agreed with us propogation it's not a  tool that they can use now we have to  look at all the other issues and see if  the Prime Minister is actually acting  within the law okay Gina may look very  good to talk to you this morning thank  you very much indeed

